	"grounds": {
		"_doc": "What a map is drawn of (LayoutGen.grounds, MapField's dual grid): the ground of a square by its character of `cells` — a string for any place, a dictionary by the place's kind, the kinds of its family, its shape (`open`, `building`, `tunnels`) — the most exact key first — with `*` for the rest (LayoutGen.ground_keys), a character not here takes the one of `.`; `order` — the grounds from the lowest layer to the highest: at a meeting of grounds the higher one lies over; `sharp` — a ground whose edge stays on the square's border (walls), the others meet by a rough line between the squares' centres; `patches` — by the same keys (the first that has rows; an empty list — none), patches of another ground over the floor's own ground: `share` of the floor in blobs of about `cell` squares by the map's seed, or `near` — a rim of `width` squares round the squares of that character (a beach); `props` — a thing drawn on the square by the character and the same keys; `repeat` — squares one texture spans; `colour` — a ground with no texture yet; `edges` — pairs of grounds whose meeting is drawn (a sheet of the 16 dual-grid tiles, assets/tiles/edges/<low>__<high>.png, its alpha the line between them), the rest meet by the mask; `edge_layout` — the 5×5 corners the sheet is laid on (1 — the higher ground), its sixteen 2×2 windows each case once; `edge_band` — how wide the drawn edge lies on both sides of the line. Textures: assets/tiles/ground/<id>.png, things: assets/tiles/props/<id>.png (tools/tiles/gen_tiles.py).",
